        </navPoint>
        <navPoint class="chapter" id="num_740" playOrder="707">
          <navLabel>
            <text>Chapter 13 The circulation and exchange of goods and merchandise as well as their production are carried on in Europe by undertakers, and at a risk</text>
          </navLabel>
          <content src="text/part0223_split_013.html#chapter_en_13"/>
        </navPoint>
        <navPoint class="chapter" id="num_741" playOrder="708">
          <navLabel>
            <text>Chapter 14 The fancies, the fashions, and the modes of living of the prince, and especially of the landowners, determine the use to which land is put in a state and cause the variations in the market prices of all things</text>
          </navLabel>
          <content src="text/part0223_split_014.html#chapter_en_14"/>
        </navPoint>
        <navPoint class="chapter" id="num_742" playOrder="709">
